hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1727","**
Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Ḥujr al-Sa‘dī,
Narrated to us Ismā‘īl—meaning Ibn Ja‘far—
Narrated to us al-‘Alā.

And it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd,
Narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad—meaning Ibn Qays al-Madanī—
Narrated to us al-‘Alā ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān.

And it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Bashshār,
And narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Ja‘far.

And it was narrated to us Abū Mūsā,
Narrated to me Muḥammad ibn Ja‘far,
Narrated to us Shu‘bah—
Qālah Bundār: from al-‘Alā.
And Abū Mūsā said: I heard al-‘Alā say:

And it was narrated to us Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd Allāh ibn Bazīgh,
Narrated to us Yazīd—meaning Ibn Zuray‘—
Narrated to us Rawḥ ibn al-Qāsim,
From al-‘Alā,
From his father,
From Abū Hurayrah (RA),
That the Prophet (ﷺ) said:
“There does not rise the sun on any day, nor does it set, that is more excellent or greater than the Day of Jumu‘ah. And there is no creature that is not terrified by the Day of Jumu‘ah except these two heavy ones: the jinn and mankind.”

‘Ali ibn Ḥujr, Ibn Bazī‘, and Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd said: “on a day more excellent,” and they did not doubt.

---"
